From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BananaDS <bananads@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] BananaDS: local wireless started, changed and ended while the
 game runs

Emu::lan_request() asks for Off, Host (with its size) or Join (look for hosts, or join one address) from any
thread and returns at once; the emulator's thread carries it out between two frames, or in the paused menu's
service loop, so a join that waits up to 5 s for its host never blocks the caller. Emu::lan_status() gives the
mode, the state (idle, busy, ready, failed and why), the session's players with their ping and, while looking,
the hosts melonDS's LAN discovery hears. A failed join, or a host that leaves, goes back to looking for hosts
with a message. wifi.local accepts "join" (look for hosts at the start); wifi.local_players (default 4) is
clamped to 2-16. Needs melonDS patch 0095.
---
 bananads/docs/SETTINGS.md |   4 +-
 bananads/src/emu.cpp      | 245 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 bananads/src/emu.h        |  36 ++++++
 3 files changed, 272 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

